# Branches and pull requests

Daniel Terefe is the only person who merges. Do not merge a pull request unless he asks in this conversation.

Promotion order:

1. A phase branch into `dev`. `dev` rejects a direct push.
2. `dev` into `prod`. `prod` accepts a pull request only from `dev`.
3. `prod` into `main`. `main` accepts a pull request only from `prod`.

`dev`, `prod`, and `main` are protected. Week branches are not.

Names:

- Phase branch: `phase-NN/tNN.N-short-name`, for example `phase-01/t01.6-firebase`. The phase comes first, then the task. Phase 01 is the work in `docs/phases/week-01.md`.
- Commit: `TNN.N summary (SRS ids)`, for example `T01.6 Initialise Firebase for the dev flavor (NF-08)`. A fix on that task stays on the same phase branch and names the task.
- Pull request title: `Phase NN · TNN.N summary`. The pull request targets `dev`.

There is no prod Firebase project. Crashlytics, when added, is for the dev flavor only.
